# Day 5 – Challenges

## Challenge 1 – Understanding SOQL

Initially, it was difficult to understand how to write SOQL queries
for custom Salesforce objects.

### Solution

Practiced SELECT, WHERE, ORDER BY and LIMIT using Student, Job and
Application objects.

---

## Challenge 2 – Working with Record IDs

Student and Job record IDs were required while working with
Application records.

### Solution

Used SOQL to retrieve the required record IDs.

---

## Challenge 3 – Duplicate Application Check

The system needed to prevent the same Student from applying to the
same Job more than once.

### Solution

Used a SOQL query with Student__c and Job__c to check whether an
Application already exists.

---

## Challenge 4 – Eligibility Validation

The Student CGPA had to satisfy the Job's Minimum CGPA.

### Solution

Compared:

Student CGPA >= Job Minimum CGPA

Only eligible Students can proceed with the Application.

---

## Challenge 5 – DML Operations

Understanding when to use INSERT and UPDATE was initially confusing.

### Solution

INSERT is used when creating a new Application.

UPDATE is used when changing an existing Application, such as
changing its Status.

---

## Challenge 6 – Testing Apex

Testing Apex code and checking query results required working with
actual Salesforce records.

### Solution

Used Salesforce tools and existing Student, Job and Application
records for testing.

---

## Final Status

SOQL practice completed.

DML practice completed.

